    "body": "Do we need to be more specific here? As written, this would fire \"cancel\" if a user selected a file, clicked OK, re-opened the file picker, selected the same file again, and clicked OK. In that case, the selection \"would not be changed\". Is that intentional? If so, perhaps this case could be explicitly folded into the new note below.",
